The provided class `ObservableIgnoreElementsCompletable` is a thin wrapper around an existing `ObservableSource` that merely forwards lifecycle events while discarding emitted items. Its behavior is trivial and deterministic, involving no computationally intensive logic or algorithmic complexity. Consequently, a JMH microbenchmark would not yield insightful performance data beyond measuring the inherent overhead of RxJava's subscription mechanics, which is better evaluated in the context of larger reactive pipelines rather than this isolated operator. Therefore, generating a dedicated JMH benchmark for this specific class is unnecessary.